s determinants of mitochondrial Ca<sup>2+</sup> responses</article-title><source>Science.</source><volume>280</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>1763</fpage><lpage>1766</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9624056</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Robb-Gaspersetal1998"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Robb-Gaspers</surname><given-names>L.D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Burnett</surname><given-names>P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Rutter</surname><given-names>G.A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Denton</surname><given-names>R.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Rizzuto</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>A.P.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Integrating cytosolic calcium signals into mitochondrial metabolic responses</article-title><source>EMBO (Eur. Mol. Biol. Organ.) J.</source><volume>17</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>4987</fpage><lpage>5000</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="RooneyandMeldolesi1996"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rooney</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Meldolesi</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The endoplasmic reticulum in PC12 cells. Evidence for a mosaic of domains differently specialized in Ca<sup>2+</sup> handling</article-title><source>J. Biol. Chem.</source><volume>271</volume><year>1996</year><fpage>29304</fpage><lpage>29311</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8910591</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Rutteretal1996"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rutter</surname><given-names>G.A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Burnett</surname><given-names>P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Rizzuto</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Brini</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Murgia</sur